{{!
    @template theme_dimensions/category_pages

    The "Pages of this area" strip: the category's local_page pages the viewer
    may read, as compact links in the toolbar's chip skin, under the hero and
    above the toolbar - outside what a search or a filter rewrites. Drawn only
    when local_page is installed and names a page; the plugin decides who may
    read what (classes/output/category_pages.php asks it).

    The name and the description arrive in the plain spelling and are escaped
    here, once. The description is the link's title rather than text of its
    own, which keeps the links compact and leaves the page name as the link's
    accessible name.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "label": "Páginas desta área",
        "pages": [
            {
                "name": "Edital 2026",
                "url": "https://example.com/r.php/local_page/category/7/edital-2026",
                "description": "Regras e prazos da seleção de 2026.",
                "hasdescription": true
            },
            {
                "name": "Calendário & contatos",
                "url": "https://example.com/r.php/local_page/category/7/calendario",
                "description": "",
                "hasdescription": false
            }
        ]
    }
}}
<nav class="dim-pages" data-region="dim-pages" aria-labelledby="dim-pages-label">
    <span class="dim-pages__label" id="dim-pages-label">{{label}}</span>
    <ul class="dim-pages__list">
        {{#pages}}
        <li class="dim-pages__item">
            <a class="dim-pages__link" href="{{url}}" data-region="dim-pages-link"{{#hasdescription}} title="{{description}}"{{/hasdescription}}>
                <span class="dim-pages__name">{{name}}</span>
                <i class="fa fa-arrow-right dim-pages__glyph" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            </a>
        </li>
        {{/pages}}
    </ul>
</nav>
